   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "One more stroke: the «y»",
     "texto": [
      "If you add a short stroke to a vowel, a «y» is placed in front of it: ㅏ (a) → **ㅑ (ya)**, ㅓ (ŏ) → **ㅕ (yŏ)**, ㅗ (o) → **ㅛ (yo)**, ㅜ (u) → **ㅠ (yu)**."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "The «e» sound and combined vowels",
     "texto": [
      "ㅐ and ㅔ nowadays sound the same: **e**. With a «y» added, ㅒ and ㅖ = **ye**.",
      "Vowels can also combine: ㅗ + ㅏ = **ㅘ (wa)**, ㅜ + ㅓ = **ㅝ (wŏ)**, ㅜ + ㅣ = **ㅟ (wi)**.",
      "ㅚ, ㅙ and ㅞ all sound **weh**.",
      "ㅢ is ㅡ + ㅣ: **ŭi**, said quickly."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
